  "scope": "Comparator acceptance and fixture names are not conformity evidence. Every successful page must match its dimensions and packed-pixel hash; rejection cases are not bitmap passes. The two nonprogress cases retain exact100000-unit-cap errors and additionally require identical default-budget Work errors within3seconds in every supported API shape. This is a finite regression deadline, not a portable latency guarantee. Expected successes report the named recovery or an empty list for conforming input. Strict uses fresh/context bytes and the original Decoder reader; Compatibility uses only Decoder/Context bytes. Contexts are reused for a second decode; no assumed I/O proof interface is added.",
